invariant: INV-7
file: quic.c
catches: quic_driver_test
reason: ch_quic_retry_ok checks every Retry under the session's
  original version instead of the version the packet names, so a Retry
  in another version validates, where RFC 9369 section 4.1 makes a
  client ignore it (rfc9369.txt:221-222). test/quic_version_tests.h
  requires 0 for a tag minted in version 1 and named as any other
  version.

--- old
    if (version != q->t.cfg.quic_original_version) {
        return 0;
    }
    return quic_retry_ok(version, pseudo, n, tag);
--- new
    (void)version;
    return quic_retry_ok(q->t.cfg.quic_original_version, pseudo, n, tag);
